# Dev-Mac chat model for libs/models `dev_mac` backend (DEP-S0, Sprint L1).
#
# Why a Modelfile: Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint ignores per-request
# `num_ctx`, and the default context (4k) silently truncates a transcript
# window. Baking num_ctx into a named model is the only way the /v1 route
# honours the `context_window` promised in config/models.yaml.
#
# Why 16K (Sprint L1 T1): the pipeline's calls are small — a 6 000-character
# window (~2.5k tokens) plus ~1.2k of system prompt and up to 3k of output;
# a reduce over a block of facts is ~4k in and 2.5k out. 32K of KV cache
# is what stopped a 12B model fitting next to the Docker dev stack on a
# 24 GB Mac. Only the eval's single-pass arm needs the long context: that
# is Modelfile.longctx, served as `notes-chat-long`.
#
# `make dev-model` runs: ollama create notes-chat -f infra/models/dev-mac/Modelfile
# Override the base with DEV_MAC_BASE_MODEL (the script substitutes FROM).
FROM gemma3:4b
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
PARAMETER temperature 0
